      <target>11</target>\n    </configuration>\n</plugin>\n```\n\n**Impact:**\nWithout updating the plugin and target version, the application will continue compiling as Java 11 bytecode, missing Java 17 optimizations, performance improvements, and language features.\n\n**Recommended Fix:**\n```xml\n<plugin>\n    <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>\n    <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>\n    <version>3.11.0</version>\n    <configuration>\n        <source>17</source>\n        <target>17</target>\n        <release>17</release>\n    </configuration>\n</plugin>\n```\n\n**Effort:** Low (5-10 minutes)\n\n---\n\n#### Issue 2: Maven Compiler Properties Need Java 17 Update [MEDIUM SEVERITY]\n**Location:** `pom.xml:13-15`  \n**Category:** Build Configuration  \n**Breaking Change:** Yes\n\n**Problem:**\nThe Maven properties specify Java 11 as the source and target version. This is the root configuration that needs updating.\n\n**Current Code:**\n```xml\n<properties>\n    <maven.compiler.source>11</maven.compiler.source>\n    <maven.compiler.target>11</maven.compiler.target>\n    <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>\n</properties>\n```\n\n**Impact:**\nThe build system will continue treating this as a Java 11 project, preventing use of Java 17 features and optimizations.\n\n**Recommended Fix:**\n```xml\n<properties>\n    <maven.compiler.source>17</maven.compiler.source>\n    <maven.compiler.target>17</maven.compiler.target>\n    <maven.compiler.release>17</maven.compiler.release>\n    <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>\n    <java.version>17</java.version>\n</properties>\n```\n\n**Effort:** Low (2-5 minutes)\n\n---\n\n#### Issue 3: Spring Boot Version Should Be Upgraded [HIGH SEVERITY]\n**Location:** `pom.xml:25`  \n**Category:** Framework Compatibility  \n**Breaking Change:** Yes (if upgrading to 3.x)\n\n**Problem:**\nSpring Boot 2.7.0 technically supports Java 17, but Spring Boot 3.x is the recommended version for optimal Java 17 support. Spring Boot 3.x uses Jakarta EE 9+ (jakarta.* packages) instead of Java EE (javax.* packages).\n\n**Current Code:**\n```xml\n<dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n    <version>2.7.0</version>\n</dependency>\n```\n\n**Impact:**\nThe application will work with Spring Boot 2.7.0 on Java 17, but you'll miss:\n- Performance optimizations specific to Java 17\n- Native compilation support (GraalVM)\n- Better observability features\n- Future security updates (2.x enters maintenance mode)\n\n**Short-term Solution (Lower Effort):**\nUpdate to the latest Spring Boot 2.7.x release:\n```xml\n<dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n    <version>2.7.18</version>\n</dependency>\n```\n\n**Long-term Solution (Recommended but Higher Effort):**\nUpgrade to Spring Boot 3.2.x:\n```xml\n<parent>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n    <version>3.2.0</version>\n</parent>\n\n<dependencies>\n    <dependency>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n    </dependency>\n</dependencies>\n```\n\n**Note:** Upgrading to Spring Boot 3.x requires changing `javax.*` imports to `jakarta.*`, which affects Servlet, Persistence, Validation, and other Java EE APIs. This is significant effort but provides the best long-term support.\n\n**Effort:**  \n- Short-term (2.7.18): Low (10 minutes)\n- Long-term (3.2.x): High (2-4 hours for javax to jakarta migration)\n\n---\n\n#### Issue 4: MySQL Connector Should Use New Artifact Name [HIGH SEVERITY]\n**Location:** `pom.xml:20`  \n**Category:** Maven Dependencies  \n**Breaking Change:** No (artifact rename only)\n\n**Problem:**\nMySQL has renamed their connector artifact from `mysql:mysql-connector-java` to `com.mysql:mysql-connector-j`. While version 8.0.33 supports Java 17, using the old artifact name may cause issues with future updates.\n\n**Current Code:**\n```xml\n<dependency>\n    <groupId>mysql</groupId>\n    <artifactId>mysql-connector-java</artifactId>\n    <version>8.0.33</version>\n</dependency>\n```\n\n**Impact:**\nThe current version works fine with Java 17, but:\n- Future security patches may only be released under the new artifact name\n- The old artifact is considered legacy\n- May cause confusion in dependency management\n\n**Recommended Fix:**\n```xml\n<dependency>\n    <groupId>com.mysql</groupId>\n    <artifactId>mysql-connector-j</artifactId>\n    <version>8.2.0</version>\n</dependency>\n```\n\n**Effort:** Low (5 minutes)\n\n---\n\n#### Issue 5: Legacy JDBC Driver Loading Pattern [MEDIUM SEVERITY]\n**Location:** `src/main/java/com/test/DatabaseService.java:40`  \n**Category:** Deprecated APIs  \n**Breaking Change:** No\n\n**Problem:**\nThe code explicitly loads the JDBC driver using `Class.forName()`, which has been unnecessary since JDBC 4.0 (Java 6). Modern JDBC drivers auto-register via the Service Provider Interface (SPI).\n\n**Current Code:**\n```java\n// BLOCKER: Hardcoded JDBC driver\nClass.forName(\"com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver\");\n\n// BLOCKER: Hardcoded connection string and credentials\nconnection = DriverManager.getConnection(DB_URL, DB_USERNAME, DB_PASSWORD);\n```\n\n**Impact:**\nThis is legacy code that continues to work in Java 17 but is redundant. The driver will auto-load when `DriverManager.getConnection()` is called. No functional impact, but represents outdated coding practices.\n\n**Recommended Fix:**\n```java\n// Driver auto-loads in JDBC 4.0+ - no explicit loading needed\n// Remove: Class.forName(\"com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver\");\n\nconnection = DriverManager.getConnection(DB_URL, DB_USERNAME, DB_PASSWORD);\n```\n\n**Effort:** Low (2 minutes)\n\n---\n\n### Build Tool Analysis\n\n**Current Build Tool:** Maven  \n**Build Configuration File:** `pom.xml`\n\n**Current State:**\n- Maven compiler plugin: 3.8.1 (outdated)\n- Source/Target version: 11\n- No `release` parameter specified\n- Missing `java.version` property\n\n**Required Changes:**\n\n1. **Update Compiler Properties:**\n```xml\n<properties>\n    <maven.compiler.source>17</maven.compiler.source>\n    <maven.compiler.target>17</maven.compiler.target>\n    <maven.compiler.release>17</maven.compiler.release>\n    <java.version>17</java.version>\n    <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>\n</properties>\n```\n\n2. **Update Maven Compiler Plugin:**\n```xml\n<plugin>\n    <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>\n    <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>\n    <version>3.11.0</version>\n    <configuration>\n        <source>17</source>\n        <target>17</target>\n        <release>17</release>\n    </configuration>\n</plugin>\n```\n\n3. **Recommended: Add Surefire Plugin for Testing:**\n```xml\n<plugin>\n    <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>\n    <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>\n    <version>3.2.2</version>\n</plugin>\n```\n\n---\n\n### Dependency Analysis\n\n**Currently Used Dependencies:**\n1. `mysql:mysql-connector-java:8.0.33` - Compatible with Java 17 but uses legacy artifact name\n2. `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-web:2.7.0` - Compatible with Java 17 but not optimized\n\n**No Incompatible Dependencies Found** - All current dependencies work with Java 17.\n\n**Recommended Dependency Updates:**\n\n| Dependency | Current Version | Recommended Version | Priority | Reason |\n|------------|----------------|---------------------|----------|---------|\n| mysql-connector-java | 8.0.33 | 8.2.0 (new artifact) | High | Migrate to new artifact name `com.mysql:mysql-connector-j` |\n| spring-boot-starter-web | 2.7.0 | 2.7.18 (short-term)<br>3.2.0+ (long-term) | High | Better Java 17 support and security updates |\n| maven-compiler-plugin | 3.8.1 | 3.11.0 | High | Required for proper Java 17 compilation |\n\n---\n\n### Code Analysis Summary\n\n**Total Java Files Analyzed:** 2\n- `src/main/java/com/test/DatabaseService.java` (92 lines)\n- `src/main/java/com/test/MiniApp.java` (84 lines)\n\n**Java Language Features Used:**\n- Standard Java I/O (File, FileInputStream)\n- JDBC Database connectivity\n- ServerSocket networking\n- Properties configuration\n- Exception handling (try-catch)\n\n**Good News:**\n✅ No usage of removed Java 11→17 APIs  \n✅ No deprecated Java APIs that break in Java 17  \n✅ No module system conflicts detected  \n✅ No javax.* packages that require Jakarta migration (in application code)  \n✅ Code uses standard Java SE APIs that are stable across versions  \n\n**Code Compatibility:** The Java source code is 100% compatible with Java 17. No code changes are required beyond the optional removal of the legacy JDBC driver loading pattern.\n\n---\n\n### Upgrade Readiness Assessment\n\n**Overall Readiness: READY** ✅\n\nThis application is in good shape for upgrading from Java 11 to Java 17. The code itself requires no changes - all issues are related to build configuration and dependency management.\n\n**Risk Level: LOW**\n\n**Why the upgrade will succeed:**\n1. Small codebase (only 2 Java files)\n2. No usage of deprecated/removed APIs\n3. Standard Java SE functionality\n4. Current dependencies support Java 17\n5. No complex framework interactions\n\n**Critical Path to Success:**\n1. Update POM properties to Java 17 (2 minutes)\n2. Update Maven compiler plugin to 3.11.0 (2 minutes)\n3. Update MySQL connector to new artifact (5 minutes)\n4. Run `mvn clean install` to verify build (1 minute)\n5. Run application tests (if any) to verify runtime behavior\n\n**Total Minimum Time Required: ~10-15 minutes for basic upgrade**\n\n**Optional Improvements (recommended but not required):**\n- Update Spring Boot to 2.7.18 for latest patches (10 minutes)\n- Remove legacy `Class.forName()` driver loading (2 minutes)\n- Consider Spring Boot 3.x upgrade for long-term support (2-4 hours)\n\n---\n\n### Recommendations\n\n#### Immediate Actions (Required):\n1. ✅ **Update `pom.xml` compiler properties to Java 17**\n2. ✅ **Update maven-compiler-plugin to version 3.11.0+**\n3. ✅ **Verify JAVA_HOME points to JDK 17**\n4. ✅ **Run `mvn clean install` to test the build**\n5. ✅ **Run application and verify functionality**\n\n#### Short-term Actions (Recommended):\n6. 🔹 **Update Spring Boot to 2.7.18** for latest security patches\n7. 🔹 **Migrate MySQL connector to new artifact** `com.mysql:mysql-connector-j`\n8. 🔹 **Remove legacy JDBC driver loading** (`Class.forName()`)\n9. 🔹 **Add maven-surefire-plugin** for future testing support\n\n#### Long-term Actions (Consider):\n10. 🔸 **Evaluate Spring Boot 3.x upgrade** for optimal Java 17 support\n11. 🔸 **Leverage Java 17 language features** (records, sealed classes, pattern matching)\n12. 🔸 **Consider using text blocks** for multi-line strings\n13. 🔸 **Evaluate switch expressions** for cleaner code\n14. 🔸 **Review GC options** - G1GC is default in Java 17 with improved performance\n\n---\n\n### Testing Recommendations\n\nAfter making the changes, perform these tests:\n\n1. **Build Verification:**\n```bash\nmvn clean install\n```\n\n2. **Dependency Tree Check:**\n```bash\nmvn dependency:tree\n```\n\n3. **Verify Java Version:**\n```bash\nmvn --version\njava -version\n```\n\n4. **Runtime Testing:**\n- Start the application\n- Test database connectivity\n- Verify server socket binding\n- Check file I/O operations\n- Monitor for any runtime warnings or errors\n\n5. **Look for Warnings:**\n```bash\nmvn clean install -X | grep -i warning\n```\n\n---\n\n### Complete Updated pom.xml\n\nHere's the complete updated `pom.xml` with all recommended changes for Java 17:\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\"\n         xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 h